{
 "about": "v0.3 C0 content-scanner corpus (02-email-guard.md, measurable false-positive plan). Measured by test/content-corpus.test.ts. No real mailbox content: everything is written for this repository or rendered from LaunchSafe's own templates with example data. Attack payloads are benign markers (LSTEST).",
 "groups": {
  "template": "marketing and transactional HTML templates (preheaders, responsive alternates, Outlook conditional copies, dark mode, tracking pixels) and their text parts: must never quarantine",
  "newsletter": "AI and security newsletters quoting injection phrases in visible prose: flag at most, never quarantine",
  "multilingual": "Hindi, Bengali, Persian, Arabic, Urdu, Hebrew, Japanese, Thai, Chinese, Korean, Sinhala, Malayalam, flag emoji: must never quarantine",
  "mailing_list": "list posts whose sender authentication fails on forwarding (authFail set) with nothing agent-directed: must never quarantine",
  "calendar": "invites and long agendas: must never quarantine",
  "ham": "ordinary mail and MCP tool results (JSON, Markdown, diffs, logs): must never quarantine",
  "attack": "attacks.json: every family must quarantine (recall)"
 },
 "notTheFullPlan": "The spec's E1 corpus adds the SpamAssassin ham set (6,000), public list archives and 150 open-source templates; those need downloads and per-file licence checks and belong to E1's mail-friction gate.",
